No definite new runtime defect was established, but the modified tests leave two core guarantees inadequately guarded. Review was read-only; no builds or tests were run.

Full review comments:

- [P2] Test Save Data independently of budget exhaustion — /Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/worktrees/lane-b/e2e/advance-stream.spec.ts:65-65
  On mobile/Balanced dev runs, Town assets exhaust the 12 MB allowance before contract prefetching begins. Accepting `budget-exhausted` therefore lets this test pass even if the Save Data priority filter is removed: the budget, rather than Save Data, prevents contract requests. Use small mocked responses and require `ready` so the test proves that Save Data overrides the opt-in.

- [P2] Use non-unit response sizes to verify byte accounting — /Users/robin/Claude/Projects/Gold Rush/worktrees/lane-b/e2e/advance-stream-bounded.spec.ts:105-107
  Every mocked response contains exactly one byte, and the starting balance is calculated from the number of URLs. Consequently, incorrectly incrementing the counter once per request instead of measuring response bytes would still pass every budget and reload assertion. Use known multi-byte bodies and calculate expectations from their sizes so this test distinguishes a byte allowance from a file-count limit.
